    "body": "With update to latest FFImage release 2.2.1 (From 2.1.8) our app was prevented from uploading to iTunes Connect Testflight.\r\n\r\nReason: \r\n> We have discovered one or more issues with your recent delivery for \"******\". To process your delivery, the following issues must be corrected:\r\n> \r\n> This app attempts to access privacy-sensitive data without a usage description. The app's Info.plist must contain an NSPhotoLibraryUsageDescription key with a string value explaining to the user how the app uses this data.\r\n> \r\n> Once these issues have been corrected, you can then redeliver the corrected binary.\r\n\r\nUsually i used \"Link SDK assemblies\" to get app passed (because Xamarin SDK has all the references to privacy APIs, like Siri etc), but now it does not help.",
